WEBVTT

00:12.840 --> 00:14.470
So cool!

00:14.930 --> 00:17.720
What, you want to play the guitar too now?

00:18.260 --> 00:21.350
I've never tried before...do you think I can do it?

00:23.100 --> 00:24.560
Be as cool as Momoka-san?

00:29.480 --> 00:30.230
Yeah, no.

00:30.730 --> 00:34.070
You've never touched a guitar.
It'll just distract you from singing.

00:35.570 --> 00:37.700
She's off in her own little world.

00:37.870 --> 00:41.870
Well, it's always like that after your first concert.

00:42.120 --> 00:45.040
It's definitely gotten into her head.

00:47.130 --> 00:50.460
<i>Screaming out my bottled up feelings</i>

00:51.460 --> 00:56.180
<i>as loud as possible, until I'm out of breath.</i>

01:02.220 --> 01:05.140
<i>It was the first time I did something like that.</i>

01:06.020 --> 01:09.150
<i>I was always so obsessed</i>

01:09.310 --> 01:12.570
<i>with the image people had of me...</i>

01:15.530 --> 01:16.530
Nina!

01:19.570 --> 01:20.780
Practice time.

01:23.240 --> 01:23.870
Coming!

02:55.590 --> 03:00.180
BETWEEN GRATITUDE AND SURPRISE

02:59.300 --> 03:00.590
Alright, let's stop here.

03:01.890 --> 03:03.800
- What do you think?
- Pretty good.

03:04.600 --> 03:05.510
Let's give it a listen.

03:06.060 --> 03:06.850
<i>I want to break everything</i>

03:07.020 --> 03:08.930
<i>My courage has left me</i>

03:09.100 --> 03:11.900
<i>Please, someone give me a reason to exist</i>

03:12.400 --> 03:14.020
Oooh, that sounds good.

03:14.190 --> 03:16.690
<i>There are countless</i>

03:17.110 --> 03:20.900
Nina, can you vary the pitch a bit more
at the start of the verse?

03:21.570 --> 03:26.870
<i>Please, someone give me a reason to exist</i>

03:27.040 --> 03:28.040
Like this?

03:28.450 --> 03:30.830
Yeah, it's a bit boring otherwise.

03:31.000 --> 03:33.290
Also, let's redo the drums too.

03:33.460 --> 03:35.040
Like, now?

03:35.590 --> 03:37.710
I gotta wake up early tomorrow, you know.

03:40.220 --> 03:41.590
Diamond Dust?

03:41.930 --> 03:45.760
Yeah, I saw her looking them up.
They're probably on her mind a lot.

03:46.140 --> 03:48.970
Could be, but think about it, they're real pros unlike us.

03:49.140 --> 03:50.850
Yeah, but...

03:51.140 --> 03:53.020
If she really had any regrets,

03:53.190 --> 03:55.610
she wouldn't have teamed up with a pair of amateurs.

03:56.650 --> 03:57.400
But...

04:02.780 --> 04:03.530
No way.

04:04.200 --> 04:05.280
Oh no!

04:05.870 --> 04:06.740
What's up?

04:06.950 --> 04:08.870
Sorry, I'm going back for today!

04:09.870 --> 04:11.450
See you tomorrow!

04:15.170 --> 04:18.500
-I'M IN FRONT OF THE STORE.
-SUBARU-CHAN, YOU OKAY?

04:15.580 --> 04:17.460
Not even a read receipt, huh...

04:17.630 --> 04:18.500
Definitely a boyfriend.

04:18.670 --> 04:19.500
Huh???

04:20.010 --> 04:22.380
Didn't think she had one though.

04:22.590 --> 04:24.930
Maybe she's trying to get back with her ex?

04:25.090 --> 04:26.720
No way, that's ridiculous!

04:26.890 --> 04:29.010
Why are you so prickly about it?

04:30.020 --> 04:30.930
Well, I mean...

04:32.310 --> 04:33.520
Do you really think that's it?

04:33.890 --> 04:37.150
Band girls are pretty popular, especially with band guys.

04:37.480 --> 04:40.070
We're their main prey.

04:40.230 --> 04:41.400
Prey...?

04:41.940 --> 04:43.450
You better be careful too.

04:44.610 --> 04:45.360
I'll call her.

04:45.530 --> 04:48.410
Like hell she'll answer.
We'll find out more tomorrow.

04:49.030 --> 04:52.910
Well, we can hang out with whoever we want
in our free time anyway.

04:53.790 --> 04:56.170
Hey Momoka-san, what do you think about them?

04:58.040 --> 05:00.050
You know, about Diamond Dust.

05:02.170 --> 05:03.970
Not much.

05:04.470 --> 05:05.800
What do you mean by that?

05:06.130 --> 05:08.800
I'm not feeling resentful or anything if that's what you mean.

05:09.350 --> 05:12.810
I just want the best for them.

05:13.270 --> 05:15.350
Then why did you quit?

05:19.190 --> 05:20.610
I don't want to talk about it.

05:21.110 --> 05:24.490
And you, stop getting distracted.
You have to sing, nothing more.

05:29.320 --> 05:31.580
What kind of band were you?

05:32.120 --> 05:33.700
I told you, just drop it.

05:34.120 --> 05:35.330
I want to know.

05:46.260 --> 05:47.050
Catch.

05:49.430 --> 05:51.430
We met in our high school's Light Music Club.

05:51.720 --> 05:55.430
But all of us were skilled
and passionate about it from the start.

05:55.980 --> 05:59.310
We all shared the same ambitions.
Felt like it was destiny, you know.

05:59.650 --> 06:02.690
I thought it was a miracle. It gave me chills.

06:03.190 --> 06:04.780
And I was right about the miracle part.

06:05.320 --> 06:07.320
Guess what, at the school festival,

06:07.490 --> 06:11.240
our concert was so packed, we physically
couldn't fit any more people.

06:11.450 --> 06:13.450
We ended it with a bang.

06:13.990 --> 06:17.410
After that, we decided to leave school to pursue our dream,

06:17.620 --> 06:19.920
and came here as indie musicians.

06:20.210 --> 06:22.710
We managed to get noticed by a label,

06:23.040 --> 06:25.210
and...that's when I left.

06:27.470 --> 06:28.510
Momoka-san.

06:31.340 --> 06:33.350
You could smile like that too, huh...

06:44.020 --> 06:46.650
Uh, shorry, I wasn't shleeping...

06:51.410 --> 06:54.370
Might as well have slept on my bed...

07:01.420 --> 07:02.790
It's from Subaru!

07:03.460 --> 07:04.500
Wait, what?

07:06.420 --> 07:07.760
SORRY, I'M LEAVING THE BAND!

07:06.710 --> 07:08.090
The hell?!

07:10.590 --> 07:12.760
We should probably drop it...

07:13.090 --> 07:14.260
How can you say that?

07:14.430 --> 07:18.640
We promised to do this together. We can't give up that easily!

07:19.350 --> 07:21.230
I'm not saying we should give up.

07:21.480 --> 07:23.900
If she wants to be in a band,
she'll ditch her boyfriend and come back.

07:24.310 --> 07:27.230
If we start pressuring her, it'll just get nasty.

07:27.690 --> 07:29.030
You think so?

07:29.610 --> 07:33.070
Could it be that you never had a boyfriend?

07:33.280 --> 07:34.990
Have <i>you?</i>

07:37.040 --> 07:39.160
Sorry for intruding...

07:39.580 --> 07:40.910
The heck are you doing?

07:41.210 --> 07:44.170
I don't know, this place stresses me out.

07:44.880 --> 07:47.380
You're the leader, so take charge.

07:47.550 --> 07:49.050
When exactly did I become the leader?

07:49.380 --> 07:52.880
I'm warning you, Subaru acts all annoying here and...

07:53.050 --> 07:54.390
Well, try not to get mad at her.

07:55.640 --> 07:56.180
Oh?

08:00.350 --> 08:01.390
Subaru...

08:01.560 --> 08:02.440
...-chan?

08:10.570 --> 08:13.320
This way, Grandmother.

08:25.000 --> 08:26.080
Could I be of assistance?

08:26.420 --> 08:28.130
- Subaru... - Could you be lost?

08:28.290 --> 08:31.460
Grandmother, I'll just give them
directions and come back...

08:34.470 --> 08:36.260
The heck are you doing here?

08:36.430 --> 08:39.470
The heck was that message?
Of course we'll come running!

08:39.890 --> 08:42.520
We'll talk about everything later,
but you need to go for now!

08:42.680 --> 08:44.980
At least explain what's going on!

08:45.190 --> 08:46.480
I told you I-

08:46.650 --> 08:47.560
And these people are?

08:48.650 --> 08:49.520
Ah, Grandmother!

08:51.070 --> 08:53.400
They're...my friends. From acting school.

08:53.650 --> 08:54.360
Me, acting?

08:58.950 --> 09:00.740
Who <i>else</i>?

09:03.710 --> 09:07.000
It's quite lively in here, isn't it.
Enough to make my head spin.

09:07.170 --> 09:09.630
It's pretty <i>crowded</i> in here, after all...

09:11.420 --> 09:12.510
Subaru-chan.

09:13.090 --> 09:14.380
- Posture.
- Yes ma'am!

09:14.590 --> 09:17.840
I keep telling you to pay attention to your posture.

09:18.010 --> 09:22.470
A person's daily habits always show when performing.

09:22.640 --> 09:26.230
It is crucial to always maintain a good physical and mental balance.

09:26.770 --> 09:28.150
Yes, Grandmother!

09:28.480 --> 09:29.650
You two as well, I'm counting on you

09:29.810 --> 09:33.400
to correct her if she forgets again.

09:33.650 --> 09:35.280
Excuse me for a moment.

09:39.280 --> 09:40.240
Subaru-chan.

09:40.410 --> 09:41.370
Yes, I know.

09:41.530 --> 09:44.620
Is she actually Tendo Awa? Like, the actress?

09:44.790 --> 09:46.210
Woah, took you long enough.

09:46.410 --> 09:48.790
Well it took me a while to connect the dots,
I didn't know anything about Subaru until now.

09:49.040 --> 09:50.920
Yeah, she's my grandma.

09:51.090 --> 09:53.800
She suddenly said she wants to visit yesterday.

09:53.960 --> 09:56.340
Wait, so your whole family's in the acting business?

09:56.510 --> 09:58.220
Not really.

09:58.430 --> 10:00.300
My parents have normal jobs.

10:01.470 --> 10:03.310
You don't actually want to be an actress, do you?

10:03.470 --> 10:07.440
Definitely not. But the thing is, I can't just throw it at her like that.

10:07.600 --> 10:10.610
Then what was that message supposed to be?!

10:13.270 --> 10:15.490
I don't know, I just panicked, or like, you know...

10:15.650 --> 10:18.950
"To deceive your enemies, start by deceiving your friends."

10:19.950 --> 10:21.120
Yeah, right.

10:21.280 --> 10:24.490
Either way, with her that's the the minimum level of precaution.

10:24.660 --> 10:27.080
She seemed pretty nice though...

10:27.620 --> 10:30.710
Yeah, at first glance. But she's from Kyoto,

10:30.880 --> 10:34.090
so if you take what she says at face value,
you'll be in for a world of pain.

10:34.250 --> 10:35.090
Really?

10:35.340 --> 10:36.670
- Posture.
- Yes ma'am!

10:37.550 --> 10:39.180
We should start heading back now.

10:39.340 --> 10:42.890
I want to see how much your acting has improved.

10:43.100 --> 10:43.600
Okay.

10:43.760 --> 10:46.730
Would you two be willing to join us?

10:47.890 --> 10:49.100
Um...yes?

10:51.150 --> 10:52.270
W-What is it?

10:53.440 --> 10:57.240
W-Well, i-it's just that...I have feelings...for you.

11:00.530 --> 11:01.610
Don't laugh!

11:01.990 --> 11:03.490
<i>A theater exercise?</i>

11:03.870 --> 11:06.370
<i>Yes, a romantic scene.</i>

11:06.750 --> 11:09.330
<i>You are going to confess to her,</i>

11:09.500 --> 11:12.500
<i>and Subaru will be trying to win her back.</i>

11:12.670 --> 11:13.880
<i>I...see.</i>

11:16.250 --> 11:18.090
WHAT'S THIS EXERCISE?

11:16.460 --> 11:18.340
<i>Sounds wonderful!</i>

11:18.260 --> 11:21.340
IMRPOVISED ACTING!
BASICALLY JUST WING IT!!

11:18.510 --> 11:21.800
<i>Well then, let us get back to the school and give it a try.</i>

11:21.510 --> 11:22.840
LIKE HELL I CAN DO THAT!

11:21.970 --> 11:23.850
<i>Will you come as well?</i>

11:23.010 --> 11:23.800
NO WAY!

11:23.970 --> 11:24.680
CAN'T DO ANYTHING ABOUT IT AT THIS POINT

11:24.850 --> 11:25.300
NOWAYNOWAYNOWAY!!

11:25.450 --> 11:25.900
JUST GIVE UP!

11:26.050 --> 11:26.700
ARE YOU KIDDING ME?!

11:27.970 --> 11:28.850
<i>No thank you.</i>

11:33.940 --> 11:36.480
<i>I think Nina-san must've misheard you.</i>

11:37.070 --> 11:39.110
JUST SHUT UP AND COME DAMN IT!

11:39.690 --> 11:41.950
DO YOU WANT ME TO STAY IN THE BAND OR NOT?

11:42.490 --> 11:43.620
I CAN'T DO IT!

11:44.280 --> 11:47.240
<i>Improvised acting means no prior discussion.</i>

11:47.990 --> 11:48.700
<i>Yes ma'am!</i>

11:49.540 --> 11:51.750
<i>Then let us head back.</i>

11:54.170 --> 11:54.920
Wait!

11:55.460 --> 11:56.630
You are...

11:57.590 --> 12:00.380
I don't wish to lie to myself anymore!

12:01.470 --> 12:03.890
I also love you with all my heart!

12:08.770 --> 12:10.730
Then why did you leave me?

12:11.020 --> 12:11.600
Excuse me?

12:12.310 --> 12:15.150
I took our relationship seriously from the start.

12:15.310 --> 12:17.570
I always thought we'd be together forever.

12:17.770 --> 12:20.740
So how could you just leave me so easily?

12:21.320 --> 12:21.900
Well...

12:22.070 --> 12:23.150
Answer me!

12:23.320 --> 12:26.320
Was everything you told me just a lie?

12:26.490 --> 12:29.910
No, I...I really did mean it, but...

12:30.200 --> 12:31.870
Then why?!

12:48.100 --> 12:51.390
Taking it out on me through acting was a low blow!

12:51.730 --> 12:53.270
I don't see the problem here.

12:53.480 --> 12:54.440
Put yourself in my shoes.

12:54.690 --> 12:56.940
I don't actually want to leave the band or anything.

12:57.110 --> 12:58.610
In the acting world,

12:58.940 --> 13:02.440
I'm nothing more than Tendo Awa's granddaughter.

13:02.780 --> 13:04.030
- It's just that...
- What is it?

13:06.240 --> 13:07.490
Something's not right.

13:07.700 --> 13:10.240
My grandmother never shows up unexpectedly.

13:10.490 --> 13:13.960
It's not like her, she's not spontaneous.

13:18.630 --> 13:19.500
Mystery solved!

13:21.920 --> 13:23.210
<i>Girls Band Cry.</i>

13:24.470 --> 13:26.090
You got a role in a drama??

13:26.260 --> 13:29.010
MY EARS! Don't yell into the microphone!

13:29.180 --> 13:32.350
I can't do anything about it, my grandma got me the role.

13:32.520 --> 13:36.100
It's a small role, so it'll only take a week or so,

13:36.690 --> 13:38.100
but no rehearsals for me until it's done.

13:38.400 --> 13:39.060
Got it.

13:39.230 --> 13:40.110
Are you okay with that?

13:40.440 --> 13:43.990
You skip rehearsals to study too, don't you?

13:44.240 --> 13:45.740
That's different.

13:45.990 --> 13:47.490
- It's the same thing!
- No it's not!

13:51.200 --> 13:52.450
Stop fighting.

13:52.620 --> 13:55.370
But Subaru-chan might leave at this rate!

13:55.910 --> 13:57.500
That's par for the course in a band.

13:57.710 --> 13:58.750
But I don't want her to...

13:58.960 --> 14:00.500
Why are you even sulking?

14:00.840 --> 14:03.250
Because you don't seem to care, that's why.

14:03.460 --> 14:06.680
From where I stand, you're the one that doesn't seem to care.

14:06.840 --> 14:08.760
I'm saying I'll come back.

14:08.930 --> 14:10.390
Trust me!

14:10.760 --> 14:11.550
But...

14:12.060 --> 14:16.020
Listen, we all have things we don't want people prying into.

14:16.730 --> 14:20.020
You wouldn't want someone prying into why you came here, right?

14:20.230 --> 14:20.900
Well...

14:21.060 --> 14:22.440
We're wasting time.

14:22.610 --> 14:26.030
You can go, Nina. We're only recording the drums today.

14:28.450 --> 14:31.200
The heck's their problem?
Here I am, trying to be considerate and all...

14:31.370 --> 14:32.620
Grrrr...

14:35.370 --> 14:37.000
<i>Are you free tomorrow?</i>

14:37.370 --> 14:38.040
<i>No!</i>

14:41.130 --> 14:42.250
<i>But actually yes!</i>

14:45.550 --> 14:47.130
Where is this?...

14:47.720 --> 14:48.800
My house.

14:49.010 --> 14:50.430
Come on in.

14:50.470 --> 14:51.430
THE NEXT DAY

14:53.010 --> 14:54.430
Awesome...

14:56.020 --> 14:57.520
You'd get sick of it pretty fast.

14:58.020 --> 14:59.810
- Is tea fine?
- Yeah.

15:00.480 --> 15:02.480
You can sit wherever you'd like.

15:08.150 --> 15:10.070
That one's great for playing games.

15:10.320 --> 15:11.110
Thank you.

15:12.240 --> 15:13.160
Look at this.

15:17.120 --> 15:18.830
She's so pretty...

15:20.000 --> 15:24.460
I wanted to talk to you properly before you
start getting all grumpy on me again.

15:25.000 --> 15:27.090
STARRING TENDO AWA

15:28.170 --> 15:34.470
SUBARU

15:29.050 --> 15:32.140
That movie's where my name comes from.

15:32.300 --> 15:34.350
My grandmother chose it.

15:35.060 --> 15:37.430
Wait, don't tell me that's...

15:38.020 --> 15:42.310
Yep. Apparently,
that movie launched her career.

15:42.480 --> 15:45.320
It was long before I was born.

15:48.320 --> 15:50.400
To her, this name was meant to bring me luck,

15:51.400 --> 15:52.820
if I ever wanted to become an actor.

15:54.820 --> 15:56.700
But you don't.

15:56.990 --> 15:57.950
Exactly.

15:58.120 --> 16:02.040
I'll always be given special treatment because of my grandmother.

16:02.210 --> 16:05.340
And besides, I don't like pretending to be someone.
It's embarrassing.

16:09.300 --> 16:10.090
But you know,

16:10.920 --> 16:12.880
when I tell her that I'm still aiming to become an actress,

16:13.430 --> 16:14.510
she genuinely smiles.

16:15.010 --> 16:17.760
Without putting on an act.

16:18.180 --> 16:19.720
Not with a fake smile.

16:31.950 --> 16:32.860
So, what do you think?

16:33.990 --> 16:35.700
If it were you, what you would do?

16:37.580 --> 16:38.240
Here.

16:39.790 --> 16:42.160
Got it through your thick skull a bit better now?

16:42.910 --> 16:45.540
But...you can't keep things as they are.

16:45.710 --> 16:49.000
If you're not going to become an actress,
you should tell her that as soon as possible.

16:49.500 --> 16:50.590
I know, right?

16:52.760 --> 16:53.800
You really should.

16:55.930 --> 16:58.850
I was hoping that if I went to acting school,
she'd just see that I don't have the talent for it

16:59.010 --> 17:01.470
and give up at some point...

17:03.350 --> 17:04.850
See you later.

17:05.650 --> 17:07.400
And don't worry, I'm not gonna leave the band.

17:07.570 --> 17:08.900
Really?

17:10.030 --> 17:12.400
That concert made me realize,

17:12.550 --> 17:15.900
I kinda like playing the drums.

17:21.660 --> 17:24.290
I'm trying to open up to you here, say something you little-

17:28.380 --> 17:29.250
<i>What's this?</i>

17:34.920 --> 17:37.260
I'M SORRY. - NINA

17:39.720 --> 17:42.890
If you're gonna feel bad about it,
don't throw a fit in the first place.

17:44.180 --> 17:49.310
A FEW DAYS LATER

17:44.180 --> 17:47.480
And here we have the main character of
<i>Detective Grandma's Case Files</i> Part 6,

17:47.650 --> 17:49.310
the famous Tendo Awa-san!

17:50.570 --> 17:51.690
I'll be in your care.

17:52.030 --> 17:55.320
I'm her granddaughter, Subaru.
I'll be playing the role of a cashier.

17:55.490 --> 17:56.860
I'll be in your care.

17:59.740 --> 18:01.950
That's a lot of makeup.

18:02.120 --> 18:04.290
That much is necessary if you want to stand out.

18:04.540 --> 18:06.710
Bands can go pretty hard on that front too, you know.

18:07.290 --> 18:09.960
- So you wear makeup too?
- Depends on the occasion.

18:11.540 --> 18:12.800
Don't start imagining it now.

18:13.710 --> 18:14.710
Action!

18:15.670 --> 18:17.090
Is Subaru really going to tell her?

18:17.470 --> 18:19.090
Yeah, she said she would.

18:19.260 --> 18:21.220
She said she'll probably have to quit acting school

18:22.010 --> 18:25.100
and go back to live with her parents,
but she wants to stay in our band.

18:25.390 --> 18:29.600
Will it really be that big a deal?
Maybe she should keep quiet for now if it's that bad.

18:29.980 --> 18:31.150
You're not wrong.

18:31.310 --> 18:34.360
But she knows she'll have to say it someday.

18:34.980 --> 18:36.320
Cut!

18:38.240 --> 18:39.320
Let's check it.

18:40.410 --> 18:41.450
Was that it?

18:42.660 --> 18:44.740
Yes, we're done for today.

18:45.500 --> 18:47.370
It was our first collaboration.

18:47.540 --> 18:48.710
You must be happy.

18:49.790 --> 18:51.380
It has always been my dream,

18:53.840 --> 18:56.460
to share the stage with Subaru.

18:59.630 --> 19:02.010
Do you want her to become an actress?

19:02.300 --> 19:03.220
Of course.

19:04.180 --> 19:08.770
After all, she got her name
from the role that changed my life.

19:09.390 --> 19:13.360
You know,
my daughter always deeply
hated this line of work.

19:13.610 --> 19:15.320
She'd always complain about me trying to push her into it,

19:15.480 --> 19:18.780
even though I was never there for her at home.

19:19.490 --> 19:21.490
So you can imagine my happiness

19:21.820 --> 19:25.290
when Subaru said she loved acting.

19:27.000 --> 19:29.290
She was the only one who smiled at me.

19:29.540 --> 19:33.000
The only one to find value in what I was doing.

19:33.540 --> 19:37.300
When she said she wants to try it herself,
I was truly thankful.

19:38.170 --> 19:39.300
Cut!

19:39.550 --> 19:40.550
Let's check it.

19:42.010 --> 19:44.550
Well, let's see how it went.

19:47.430 --> 19:48.560
Grandmother!

19:49.930 --> 19:51.100
Great job.

19:53.610 --> 19:56.150
Um, could I talk to you for a minute?

19:56.780 --> 19:58.490
What is it?

19:59.280 --> 20:04.160
It's not urgent, but I wouldn't want you
to miss your train either.

20:04.660 --> 20:07.160
Yes, I should probably get going soon.

20:07.910 --> 20:08.660
I see.

20:09.830 --> 20:11.160
Alright, I'll say it then.

20:11.670 --> 20:12.470
You see...

20:14.830 --> 20:15.420
it's just that...

20:16.210 --> 20:17.750
I...

20:20.050 --> 20:20.800
Grandmother.

20:22.130 --> 20:22.720
I...

20:25.680 --> 20:26.430
Well...

20:26.600 --> 20:28.470
Subaru-chan, trouble!

20:29.390 --> 20:31.940
We forgot something! Come quick!

20:33.480 --> 20:36.190
No time to waste. Let's go!

20:36.360 --> 20:39.530
Huh, what? Hey! Wait!

20:41.070 --> 20:42.360
Wait, don't push me!

20:43.860 --> 20:45.410
Stop, what are you-

20:47.620 --> 20:49.450
You little hypocrite!

20:49.950 --> 20:50.700
<i>I'm sorry!</i>

20:51.250 --> 20:52.040
Shut it!

20:52.210 --> 20:56.000
You were the one who told me
to clear things up!

20:56.170 --> 20:58.710
- Well...yeah!
- Don't just agree, say something!

20:59.050 --> 21:00.960
And after I finally prepared myself for it!

21:01.340 --> 21:04.970
Well, it's just that...you know,
everyone has their share of problems and stuff.

21:05.150 --> 21:06.150
Huh??

21:06.680 --> 21:08.600
You need to be able to like, put yourself in others' shoes,

21:08.700 --> 21:10.720
and understand that things might be tough for them too and stuff.

21:11.430 --> 21:13.140
- You get me?
- Listen here you little!!

21:13.310 --> 21:14.850
It hurts!

21:15.020 --> 21:18.690
Unlike you, I've been taking that into account all along!

21:18.860 --> 21:19.860
And you just...

21:20.780 --> 21:22.740
Still, one day you'll have to tell her.

21:23.450 --> 21:23.990
When is that?

21:24.860 --> 21:27.620
When you find something you want to do.

21:28.200 --> 21:29.660
The heck is wrong with this girl?!

21:29.910 --> 21:31.120
<i>I don't know.</i>

21:34.290 --> 21:35.620
I'm done!

21:35.960 --> 21:38.000
Done, done, done and done!

21:38.590 --> 21:41.550
I steeled my resolve because you wanted me to stay,

21:41.880 --> 21:45.050
And now, I'm stuck between a flip-flopping
self-righteous prick

21:46.180 --> 21:48.430
and an apathetic know-it-all!

21:51.260 --> 21:54.390
I can handle my stuff on my own,
just leave me alone!

21:55.560 --> 21:57.060
Subaru-chan...

22:04.440 --> 22:06.280
So, how's <i>that</i> for some acting?

22:06.610 --> 22:08.200
Phew, I feel better now.

22:08.820 --> 22:12.410
I know that I'll have to
do it sooner or later.

22:12.950 --> 22:16.410
But until then,
I have your two butts to kick up!

22:18.000 --> 22:20.000
Alright, here we go!

22:27.340 --> 22:29.840
Nina Iseri: Rina
Momoka Kawaragi: Yûri

22:31.430 --> 22:34.810
Subaru Awa: Mirei
Tendo Awa: Naoko Kôda

23:47.840 --> 23:49.970
<i>To be continued: "Raise your voice."</i>
